  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "What condition is required for \\(x^2+y^2+Dx+Ey+F=0\\) to represent a circle with a positive radius?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(D^2+E^2-4F<0\\)",
    "B": "\\(D^2+E^2-4F>0\\)",
    "C": "\\(F\\) must equal 0",
    "D": "\\(D\\) and \\(E\\) must be 0"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "For real coefficients \\(D,E,F\\), completing the square reveals the squared radius:\n\\[\n\\left(x+\\frac{D}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(y+\\frac{E}{2}\\right)^2\n=\\frac{D^2+E^2-4F}{4}.\n\\]\nAfter completing the square, the right-hand side must be positive for the radius to be positive. If it equals 0, the equation represents a point; if it is less than 0, there is no real locus. Since \\(4>0\\), the required condition is \\(D^2+E^2-4F>0\\), choice B.",
